{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) issued a stitch task (#5637) to create differential tests for `cmd/vidir` (the vidir utility from moreutils). The task requires implementing `cmd/vidir/vidir_test.go` with differential tests comparing the Go vidir binary against the Homebrew moreutils reference binary. The tests must cover srd114-vidir requirements R2.1 (exit codes: exit 0 on success, exit 1 on editor failure or rename/delete failure) and R2.2 (SIGPIPE handling). Acceptance criteria require: TestDiff function exists, tests pass when reference binary available, tests skip gracefully when reference binary missing, go vet passes, and all R2.1/R2.2 test cases are present as DiffTest entries.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: build Go binary via `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`, find reference via `exec.LookPath(\"vidir\")` (no g-prefix for moreutils), compare via `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - vidir is interactive (invokes $EDITOR) — tests must override EDITOR env var with non-interactive commands\n   - vidir reads filenames from stdin when stdin is piped (not a terminal), bypassing directory listing\n   - vidir's primary output is filesystem side effects (renames/deletions), not stdout — tests must focus on exit codes and stderr\n   - DiffTest struct fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   - LC_ALL=C must be set for deterministic locale-independent output\n   - SIGPIPE handling tested via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd114-vidir.yaml`\n     - Defines the full SRD for vidir: R1 (directory editing), R2 (exit codes and SIGPIPE)\n     - R2.1: Exit 0 on success, exit 1 when editor exits non-zero or rename/delete fails\n     - R2.2: Handle SIGPIPE gracefully using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n     - Non-goals: no recursive editing, no undo\n   \n   - `cmd/vidir/main.go` (248 lines, full implementation)\n     - Key functions: `run()`, `parseFlags()`, `collectFiles()`, `isTerminalStdin()`, `readStdinFiles()`, `readDirFiles()`, `buildListing()`, `editListing()`, `writeTempFile()`, `runEditor()`, `parseListing()`, `parseLine()`, `applyChanges()`, `processRenames()`, `renameFile()`, `processDeletions()`\n     - Uses `os.Getenv(\"EDITOR\")` defaulting to \"vi\"\n     - `isTerminalStdin()` checks `os.Stdin.Stat()` for `ModeCharDevice` to decide stdin vs directory mode\n     - `makeEditorCmd(editor, path)` creates the editor command\n     - Processes renames before deletions in `applyChanges()`\n     - Verbose mode prints to stderr: `\"%s -> %s\\n\"` for renames, `\"delete %s\\n\"` for deletions\n   \n   - `cmd/pee/pee_test.go` (reference moreutils test pattern)\n     - Shows pattern: `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`, `exec.LookPath(\"pee\")`, `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n     - Includes TestSIGPIPE function as separate test\n     - Uses sortLines normalizer for non-deterministic output ordering\n     - Reference binary lookup: `exec.LookPath(\"pee\")` — no g-prefix for moreutils\n   \n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (provided in project_context)\n     - DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - RunDiffTests runs each test as a named subtest\n     - buildEnv merges test env with inherited env, sets LC_ALL=C by default\n     - checkExpectedFiles verifies filesystem state after binary execution\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - The main challenge identified is that vidir is interactive (invokes an editor). For differential testing, EDITOR must be overridden with non-interactive commands (e.g., \"true\" for no-op, \"false\" for failure, sed scripts for modifications).\n   - vidir's output is primarily filesystem side effects, not stdout. Tests should focus on: exit codes, stderr output (especially with -v), and potentially ExpectedFiles for filesystem state verification.\n   - When stdin is piped, vidir reads filenames from stdin instead of listing a directory — this can be leveraged for testing without needing actual directory contents.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive message containing the full stitch task definition including: role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, shared_protocols, package_contracts, constraints, and all configuration needed to implement the test file.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/vidir/vidir_test.go` with:\n     - TestDiff function using differential testing pattern\n     - Test cases covering R2.1 (exit 0 on success, exit 1 on editor/rename/delete failure)\n     - Test cases covering R2.2 (SIGPIPE handling)\n     - Graceful skip when reference binary \"vidir\" not found\n     - EDITOR override for non-interactive testing\n   - Verify with `go vet ./cmd/vidir/...`\n   - Verify with `go test ./cmd/vidir/... -count=1`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (srd114-vidir.yaml, cmd/vidir/main.go, cmd/pee/pee_test.go) and was about to plan the implementation approach and write `cmd/vidir/vidir_test.go`. No code has been written yet. The analysis of how to handle vidir's interactive nature in differential tests was in progress.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/vidir/vidir_test.go` following the pattern from `cmd/pee/pee_test.go`. Key design:\n   - TestDiff with `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"vidir\")` with t.Skip\n   - Test cases with EDITOR overrides (e.g., `Env: []string{\"EDITOR=true\"}` for no-op, `Env: []string{\"EDITOR=false\"}` for editor failure)\n   - Stdin-piped file lists to test listing behavior\n   - Test for nonexistent directory paths (exit 1)\n   - Test empty input (exit 0)\n   - TestSIGPIPE function similar to pee's implementation\n   - Verbose flag tests comparing stderr output\n   Then verify with `go vet` and `go test`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5637/9e7630c7-a205-448c-bfa0-74c39d48505d.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e7630c7-a205-448c-bfa0-74c39d48505d","uuid":"e4dbce4d-6939-4d46-b81a-63a08eb663e4","timestamp":"2026-05-28T17:27:25.408Z","isSynthetic":true}
